Package: dasklyr
Title: R Interface to Dask
Version: 0.1.0
Authors@R: person("Louis", "Li", email = "908163862@qq.com",
                  role = c("aut", "cre", "cph"))
Description: Run 'dplyr' verbs on Dask DataFrames from R. Connect to a
    local Dask client or a remote scheduler, copy R data frames onto the
    cluster, read and write Parquet and CSV, and collect results as
    tibbles. Computation stays in Python workers through 'reticulate';
    R only builds the graph. A Python installation with the 'dask'
    package is required (see SystemRequirements).
License: MIT + file LICENSE
Encoding: UTF-8
Language: en-US
Roxygen: list(markdown = TRUE)
Depends: R (>= 4.1)
Imports:
    dplyr,
    rlang,
    tibble,
    tidyselect,
    reticulate (>= 1.38)
Suggests:
    testthat (>= 3.0.0)
Config/testthat/edition: 3
SystemRequirements: Python with the dask (dataframe, distributed),
    pandas, and pyarrow packages
URL: https://github.com/hebian1994/dasklyr
BugReports: https://github.com/hebian1994/dasklyr/issues
Config/roxygen2/version: 8.1.0
